Automatic ClientConfig IP selection parity fix checkpoint, 2026-10-09. The macOS `getifaddrs` adapter now reverses only its IPv4 candidate sequence into the observed pinned Java `NetworkUtil.getLocalInetAddressList()` order before applying the unchanged Java selection policy; IPv6 order and generic `select` behavior remain untouched. The automatic constructor differential and macOS adapter-order unit test pass, including Java's `10.10.10.111` versus the pre-fix Rust `192.168.139.3`. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned Maven verify (22 scenarios and deterministic fixture checks), comparator self-test/manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Fixture SHA-256 `138164047171a6e1bb649d3b70239a023245341852cd4036148d80d3c722b5ea`. This is a bounded macOS IPv4 ordering correction; non-macOS enumeration and IPv6-only host selection remain under broader platform/source reconciliation. P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

